      "message": "If you unregister the listener, don\u0027t forget to ensure that the code ignores any stale callbacks that were posted before the listener was unregistered.\n\nThe usual way we do this is by storing the InterfaceObserver in a class member (e.g., mInterfaceObserver), and then in the methods inside InterfaceObserver that actually do stuff, not do anything if the observer is not the currently-registered one. Something like:\n\n    private class InterfaceObserver extends BaseNetdUnsolicitedEventListener {\n\n        ...\n\n        @Override\n        public void onInterfaceLinkStateChanged(String iface, boolean up) {\n            if (DBG) {\n                Log.i(TAG, \"interfaceLinkStateChanged, iface: \" + iface + \", up: \" + up);\n            }\n            mHandler.post(() -\u003e {\n                if (mInterfaceObserver !\u003d this) return;\n                updateInterfaceState(iface, up);\n            }\n        }",
